@startuml
title Deployment diagram: три execution environment'а

skinparam shadowing false

node "Python-процесс CLI" as proc {

  artifact "main.py" as main_art

  node "AsyncioActorDriver\n(event loop)" as async_env {
    artifact "Coordinator actors" as a_coords
    artifact "Worker actors (N)" as a_workers
    artifact "Collector actors" as a_collectors
  }

  node "ThreadedActorDriver\n(thread pool)" as threaded_env {
    artifact "Coordinator actors" as t_coords
    artifact "Worker actors (N threads)" as t_workers
    artifact "Collector actors" as t_collectors
  }

  node "ManualActorDriver\n(testing / step-by-step)" as manual_env {
    artifact "Actors driven by\nproceed() / drain()" as m_actors
  }
}

artifact "config/formats/*.yaml" as yaml_art
artifact "input document\n(*.txt / *.tex / ...)" as input_art
artifact "stdout (JSON)" as stdout_art

main_art ..> async_env : выбирает driver
main_art ..> threaded_env
main_art ..> manual_env

main_art --> yaml_art : reads
main_art --> input_art : reads
main_art --> stdout_art : writes

note bottom
  Все три environment'а реализуют один и тот же контракт ActorDriver
  (см. class/actor-drivers.puml). Выбор конкретного драйвера задаёт способ
  планирования акторов, но не их FSM-логику.
end note

@enduml
